# Build context for apps/playground is the monorepo root (the app is wired to
# @hydra-sdk/* through pnpm workspace links). Keep the context to sources only —
# host node_modules in particular must never be copied in: they carry
# platform-specific binaries built for the host, not for the image.

**/node_modules
**/.pnpm-store

# Build outputs
**/.nuxt
**/.nitro
**/.output
**/.turbo
**/.vercel
**/dist
**/.data
**/.cache

# VCS / tooling
.git
.github
.changeset
.vscode
.idea
**/.DS_Store

# Local env — .env.example stays so the image documents what it expects
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Not needed to build the playground. Note that apps/docs and apps/docs-v2 are
# NOT excluded: they are pnpm workspace members, and --frozen-lockfile checks
# every manifest the lockfile knows about. They are simply not installed (see
# the --filter in the Dockerfile).
demo
infra
docs
_bmad
_bmad-output
sdk-ai-agent
scripts
tmp
**/coverage
**/*.log
**/.playwright-mcp
